    docs: correct stats/verified_answers claims, export precondition, env/lang filters. Addresses DF-OFF-BY-ONE-9, DOC-1, DOC-2.
    
    README.md
    - Removed the false "Every answer is 100% verified (hit rate 1.0)" claim. It now says the
      exported corpus is the set of verified answers and that GET /api/v1/stats applies one
      further exclusion: answers whose signatures JSON records a failed solve are not counted
      in verified_answers, so hit_rate is computed at runtime and is not a fixed constant.
      Live numbers are printed with an observed-at-time-of-writing label.
    - Stats endpoint row in the endpoint table now states the failed-signature exclusion.
    - Scripts layout block: added scripts/pi-agent-watchdog.sh, described from the script's own
      header - it probes pi-agent WRAPPER RESOLUTION (dist/cli.js, package.json, non-empty
      node_modules/.bin, executable wrapper), is silent when healthy, and prints one deduped
      ALERT with the rebuild recipe when the binary is missing or hollowed; schedule via cron.
    
    docs/api-reference.md
    - GET /api/v1/stats: sample JSON refreshed to the live response (counts no longer equal,
      hit_rate no longer 1) and labelled as observed-at-time-of-writing; the verified_answers
      and hit_rate definition now states the failed-signature exclusion and names the
      predicate COALESCE(json_extract(signatures, '$.result'), '') != 'failed'.
    - GET /api/v1/problems: env and lang are documented as exact matches against the value
      stored on the class's answer rows, so a filter copied from the submit example
      (environment "linux") can legitimately return 0 rows; tells the reader to check the
      stored values first and cross-references the same rule for discover in integration.md.
    
    docs/integration.md
    - Export subsection: the -export-dir / 501 not_configured precondition now sits with the
      example in the same subsection (and names -import-dir for the import example), with a
      cross-reference to the Export / Import section of api-reference.md.
    - Stats sample aligned with the corrected definition, values refreshed and labelled.
    
    Measured live this session (server on :8766)
    - GET /api/v1/stats -> total_problems 1847, total_answers 2036, verified_answers 2008,
      queue_depth 0, hit_rate 0.9862475442043221, coverage 1.0871683811586357,
      avg_solve_time 2m58s, readonly false, solver_available true
    - POST /api/v1/export {"answer_ids":[42,43]} -> HTTP 501
      {"error":"not_configured","message":"export directory not configured"}
    - GET /api/v1/problems?q=raft&env=linux -> {"problems":[],"total":0}; q=raft without env
      returns the matching classes, whose answers carry env values such as go1.26
    
    Gates: go build ./... OK; go vet ./... OK; gofmt -l cmd/ internal/ pkg/ sql/ clean;
    go test ./... -short -p 1 -count=1 -timeout 120s all packages ok.
    
